The code statements that lead to the bug are:
llbitmap_state_machine(llbitmap, start, end, BitmapActionStartwrite);
llbitmap_state_machine(llbitmap, start, end, BitmapActionDiscard);
Reason:
These statements were placed before the barrier raise loop. This allowed the state machine to complete and change the bitmap state before the barrier was raised, creating a race condition where other threads could observe the new state without proper synchronization, potentially leading to inconsistent bitmap state or data corruption.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
llbitmap_state_machine(llbitmap, start, end, BitmapActionStartwrite);
llbitmap_state_machine(llbitmap, start, end, BitmapActionDiscard);
Reason:
These statements are moved after the barrier raise loop, ensuring that all necessary barriers are raised before the state machine transitions occur. This prevents the race condition by guaranteeing that any concurrent access sees the barrier before the state change is visible.

